## 3 Conclusions
In summary, we have successfully prepared ZIF-8 materials with different morphologies (cubic, truncated rhombododecahedral
and rhombododecahedral) via a thermodynamically controlled synthetic strategy. Two synthetic processes are involved in this strategy: 1) the area-reducing layered growth mode under \(30\,^{\circ}\mathrm{C}\) to obtain ZIF-8-tr and ZIF-8-r; 2) the integral layered growth mode under \(-40\,^{\circ}\mathrm{C}\) to gain ZIF-8-c. After pyrolyzing, SA-Fe/CNs inherit the morphologies and the unsaturated single sites of ZIF-8 materials. Furthermore, SA-Fe-c/CN, derived from ZIF-8-c with \(\{100\}\) facet, shows the best performance and cycling stability among SA-Fe/CNs, illustrating that ZIF-8-c with \(\{100\}\) facet and more exposed single-atom sites leads to superior ORR performance.
